 @n3me51s2  You’ve posted the same comment at least five times on this post, so I will answer, but don’t try and spam a comment next time. 

This said, I’m not the person to ask, but I can give my idea of what the issue is. While on battery mode, the PC is trying to not loose as much battery while using. Because you’re trying to play games, that demand a lot of battery and means that the PC will have to drain more in order for the demand of said game. On battery as well, the actual screen doesn’t keep up at a constant rate of fps, due to also trying not to drain as much power. 

My solution would be to try and keep it plugged in to power when you can. If you still have issues, try googling it, or even asking around on Reddit or other places to see if anyone has a solution.

